.page which 1 locate a command

# SYNOPSIS
*which* _NAME_...

# DESCRIPTION
`which` prints the full path of the program that would run for each _NAME_, searching the directories of `PATH` for an executable file. A name containing a slash is checked as it stands. Shell builtins and aliases are not known to `which`; use the `type` builtin of gapsh for those.

# EXIT STATUS
0 if every name was found, 1 otherwise.

# EXAMPLES
    which ls
    which kappabox omikuji

# SEE ALSO
type(1), env(1)
